 ['B','Oliver','My move into journalism happened almost by chance. I had written a few blog posts about local politics, and an editor happened to read one. She offered me a trial, and I simply said yes without thinking too hard about it. If I had thought it through, I probably would have turned it down, as I had no training at all.'],
 ['C','Priya','After my daughter was born, I wanted to work fewer hours, and my employer refused. So I set up my own consultancy. The first year was extremely tough, and there were months when I earned almost nothing. What got me through was a network of other self-employed parents who shared advice and, when necessary, childcare.'],
