P('L3',id='c1l3',t='Röportaj: Bir psikolog',ty='mc',sc=[('F','Today I\'m talking to psychologist Dr Sam Okafor about procrastination. Sam, why do we put things off?'),('M','The common assumption is that procrastinators are lazy, but that\'s rarely the case. Procrastination is mainly about managing emotions. We avoid tasks that make us feel anxious, bored or inadequate, and we get a short-term sense of relief.'),('F','So it\'s not a time-management problem?'),('M','Not primarily. You can give someone the best planner in the world, and if the task still makes them feel bad, they\'ll find a way to avoid it. That\'s why so many productivity apps fail.'),('F','What actually helps?'),('M','Self-compassion, surprisingly. Studies show that students who forgave themselves for procrastinating on one exam procrastinated less on the next. Being harsh on yourself just adds to the negative feelings that caused the problem.'),('F','Is there any upside to procrastination?'),('M','Some people argue that a bit of delay allows ideas to develop, and there\'s something to that. But I\'d be wary of using it as an excuse. Delaying because you\'re thinking is very different from delaying because you\'re avoiding.')],
 q=[q('According to Sam, procrastination is mainly caused by',['a lack of motivation and self-discipline.','a desire to avoid unpleasant feelings.','poor planning skills.','having too much work.'],1,['detail'],'"Procrastination is mainly about managing emotions".'),
    q('What does Sam say about productivity apps?',['They are useful for most people.','They often fail to address the real problem.','They make procrastination worse by adding pressure.','They are too complicated.'],1,['inference'],'Görev kötü hissettirdiği sürece en iyi planlayıcı da işe yaramaz.'),
    q('What does Sam recommend?',['being kinder to oneself','setting stricter deadlines','working with other people','rewarding oneself after work'],0,['detail'],'"Self-compassion".'),
    q('What is Sam\'s attitude to the idea that procrastination can be useful?',['He completely rejects it.','He accepts it without reservation.','He sees some truth in it but has doubts.','He thinks it applies only to creative people.'],2,['attitude'],'"there\'s something to that. But I\'d be wary".')]),
